.TH KINTSUGI-CHECKPOINT 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-checkpoint \- session snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi checkpoint
<id> [label]
.br
.B kintsugi checkpoint
list <id>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Snapshot a session's history as a rewind point. Checkpoints let you return to
a previous state.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP \fB<id> [label]\fR
Create a checkpoint
.IP \fBlist\fR
List checkpoints for a session
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a checkpoint:
.PP
  $ kintsugi checkpoint abc123 "before refactor"
.PP
List checkpoints:
.PP
  $ kintsugi checkpoint list abc123
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-rewind (1),
.BR kintsugi-session (1)
